1
00:00:02,627 --> 00:00:05,876
This is lab loop, our project for the Mubit hackathon.

2
00:00:05,876 --> 00:00:08,163
It's an AI lab for protein experiments

3
00:00:08,163 --> 00:00:10,931
and Mubit is what lets it learn from each run.

4
00:00:10,935 --> 00:00:13,956
We ask it to fold a thirty residue protein chain.

5
00:00:13,956 --> 00:00:18,087
Mubit memory has no lessons for this yet, so it plans from scratch.

6
00:00:18,088 --> 00:00:21,838
ESMFold returns a pTM of zero point four nine four

7
00:00:21,838 --> 00:00:26,488
under the zero point five it set for itself, so the run fails.

8
00:00:26,490 --> 00:00:30,802
The reviewer writes a lesson: that floor is too strict for a chain this short.

9
00:00:30,802 --> 00:00:32,682
The lesson goes into Mubit memory.

10
00:00:32,684 --> 00:00:34,254
We run the same task again.

11
00:00:34,254 --> 00:00:38,732
Mubit recalls the lesson, and the planner sets the floor at zero point three.

12
00:00:38,733 --> 00:00:42,813
This time it passes, and the pipeline is saved as a reusable skill.

13
00:00:49,032 --> 00:00:51,607
The Mubit gateway records every agent call

14
00:00:51,607 --> 00:00:55,776
and Mubit memory lets each run start from what earlier runs learned.
